<title>PORTUGAL: Bank/Portugal calls for strong salary restraint.</title>
<headline>Bank/Portugal calls for strong salary restraint.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Portugal said that the government could reach its 2.25-2.75 percent inflation target in 1997 but only if it imposed tough limits on salary rises and the currency remained stable.  </p>
<p>&quot;In the context of exchange rate stability this goal will only be possible with strong salary restraint,&quot; the central bank said in its latest quarterly economic report.</p>
<p>&quot;The recent trend in consumer prices and the outlook until the end of the year show there will be some resistence to be overcome (to reduce) average inflation until the end of the first quarter of 1997,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>&quot;In these circumstances progress on reducing inflation must be particularly fast in the remaining nine months of the year.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
